transport            REQUIRED  [NESTED, HIGH]
  Transport block
  kind                 REQUIRED  [STRING, HIGH]
    Transport mechanism
    one of: local, sftp, s3
  path                 optional  [STRING, HIGH]
    File path (local) or glob path (sftp)
    required when kind is local or sftp
    → Set path: /imports/*.csv (local) or a remote glob (sftp)
  host                 optional  [STRING, HIGH]
    SFTP host
    required when kind = sftp
  user                 optional  [STRING, HIGH]
    SFTP user
    required when kind = sftp
  port                 optional  [INT, LOW]
    SFTP port
    default: 22
  strict_host_key      optional  [BOOLEAN, LOW]
    Verify the SFTP host key against host_key_fingerprint
    default: true
  host_key_fingerprint optional  [STRING, MEDIUM]
    SFTP host key fingerprint (SHA256:… as ssh-keygen -lf prints it)
    required when kind is sftp and strict_host_key is not off
    → Read it with `ssh-keyscan -p <port> <host> | ssh-keygen -lf -` (the run's refusal prints the same), confirm it out of band, then set host_key_fingerprint: "SHA256:…"
  bucket               optional  [STRING, HIGH]
    S3 bucket name
    required when kind = s3
  prefix               optional  [STRING, MEDIUM]
    S3 key prefix filter
  region               optional  [STRING, MEDIUM]
    AWS region for S3
    default: eu-west-3
  endpoint             optional  [STRING, LOW]
    S3-compat endpoint (MinIO, R2)
  suffix               optional  [STRING, LOW]
    File suffix filter for s3 (empty = no filter)
  archive_path         optional  [STRING, LOW]
    Relocation target for after_process=archive|move — canonical home is spec level; a transport-level value wins if both are set (one-shot style)
  archive_bucket       optional  [STRING, LOW]
    S3 archive bucket for after_process=archive|move (default: source bucket)
  archive_prefix       optional  [STRING, LOW]
    S3 archive key prefix for after_process=archive|move
    default: archive/
  key_env              optional  [STRING, MEDIUM]
    Env var for SSH private key (SFTP)
  password_env         optional  [STRING, MEDIUM]
    Env var for SSH password (SFTP)
  access_key_env       optional  [STRING, MEDIUM]
    Env var for AWS access key (S3)
    default: AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID
  secret_key_env       optional  [STRING, MEDIUM]
    Env var for AWS secret key (S3)
    default: AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY
  at least one of key_env, password_env when kind is sftp
    → Use `lm secret set <NAME> ...` then reference it via key_env: <NAME>
  refused when given — the runtime never reads these:
    file_filter          file_filter is not read by connector runs
      → Drop it from the connector manifest
    pre_process          pre_process is not read by connector runs
      → Drop it from the connector manifest
    post_process         post_process is not read by connector runs
      → Drop it from the connector manifest
    max_file_size        max_file_size is not read by connector runs
      → Drop it from the connector manifest
parser               optional  [NESTED, HIGH]
  CSV parser config
  delimiter            optional  [STRING, LOW]
    Field delimiter (single char) — auto-detected if absent
  escape               optional  [STRING, LOW]
    Escape character for a quote inside a quoted value (single char, e.g. \) — absent means the quote is doubled (RFC 4180); DisplayTag and MySQL OUTFILE use a backslash
  encoding             optional  [STRING, LOW]
    Character encoding — auto-detected if absent
  has_header           optional  [BOOLEAN, MEDIUM]
    First row is header
    default: true
  bom_strip            optional  [BOOLEAN, LOW]
    Strip BOM from UTF-8
    default: true
  null_values          optional  [LIST, LOW]
    Strings treated as null
    default: "", "NULL", "null", "#N/A"
  lines                optional  [BOOLEAN, MEDIUM]
    One line = one row, one column (`line`): no delimiter, no quoting — fixed-width files, logs
    default: false
  short_rows           optional  [STRING, LOW]
    A line with fewer values than the declared columns: error (dead letter, default) or skip-leading (skipped while the table has not begun: a key;value block before it)
    one of: skip-leading, error
  columns              optional  [LIST, MEDIUM]
    Column names in file order
    required when has_header is false and lines is off
    → Add parser.columns: [code, name, ...] in file order
schedule             optional  [STRING, MEDIUM]
  Cron expression for recurring ingestion
after_process        REQUIRED  [STRING, MEDIUM]
  What to do after a file is processed
  one of: archive, delete, move, none
archive_path         optional  [STRING, LOW]
  Destination for `move` action
  required when after_process = move
  → Set archive_path: /path/to/archive/
mapping              optional  [NESTED, MEDIUM]
  Dataset/row/cell transformer hooks — see the transformers page
window               optional  [STRING, MEDIUM]
  Fence scheduled runs to a UTC time window, HH:MM-HH:MM (a manual run bypasses it)
refresh              optional  [NESTED, MEDIUM]
  Full refresh of one local file: the removal guard
  max_removed          optional  [STRING, MEDIUM]
    Largest share of the table one run may remove: a percentage (30% by default), or off
target               optional  [NESTED, HIGH]
  Target persistence
  indexes              optional  [LIST, LOW]
    Postgres indexes on the hub table
    → indexes is a list of { columns: [...], unique?: bool } objects — e.g. indexes: [{ columns: [email] }]
    indexes[]
      columns              REQUIRED  [LIST, HIGH]
        Columns of the index, in order
        → e.g. columns: [email] or [bpartner_id, dateordered]
      unique               optional  [BOOLEAN, LOW]
        Unique index (default false)
        default: false
